    "body": "`tsgo` refuses to attach when a `deno.json` sits in the same directory as a package manager lockfile\nand there is no `deno.lock`. The root resolver aborted when the deno root was closer than **or equal\nto** the project root, so an equal-length match, meaning both files in one directory, was read as\nDeno and the TypeScript server never started.\n\nEqual is the ambiguous case, not the Deno case. `deno.json` is also used as a plain config file by\ntools that are not Deno, which is why the absence of `deno.lock` matters here: the only positive\nevidence of a Deno project is missing, and what remains is a file that both ecosystems write.\n\nThe comparison in `lsp/ts_ls.lua` is now strict, so Deno wins only when it is genuinely closer, and an\nequal match attaches. `lsp/tsc.lua` and `lsp/vtsls.lua` carry the same resolver and are updated\ntogether, with the documentation comment describing the tie as ambiguous rather than restating the old\nrule.\n\nThe `deno.lock` branch above is untouched: a lock file is unambiguous, and it still wins.\n\nFixes #4457\n",
